+## Account for validation time
+
+Every maintained check-in gate, required CI job, and qualification has a maintainer-approved runtime target in the [shared qualification plan](scripts/ci_qualification.py), alongside the work being measured and the conditions under which the target applies. Local validation, CI, and maintained profiling scenarios use that same definition.
+
+Normal runs automatically record elapsed time, completion status, and the target comparison. Multi-stage qualifications also report phase costs, and complete validation runs report total elapsed time. Measurement is part of running the check, not an optional second task.
+
+Review that evidence before handing work back. Investigate every missed target or unavailable comparison. Do not call the work complete until the applicable targets are demonstrated or the maintainer explicitly approves proceeding with the identified shortfall. Record the evidence, decision, and any follow-up in GitHub; opening a follow-up does not itself grant approval.
+
+Changing a target, its workload, its measured interval, or its execution conditions requires explicit maintainer approval. Do not reset expectations to match a slow run or weaken required proof to improve the result.
+
+Missing or invalid required timing evidence fails validation. A valid timing miss remains report-only; it does not change the functional result or authorize changing a safety timeout.
+
+In short, **measurement and review are mandatory; unresolved misses and changed expectations require explicit approval.**
 
